{"id": "tea:katharudra-upanisad:1-rite", "source": "src:katharudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (rite)"}, "paraphrase": "The gods ask Prajāpati about renunciation; after the rite the father removes topknot and thread and tells his son 'you are Brahman, you are the sacrifice…'; the son answers 'I am Brahman…'; relatives must not shed tears, which would harm the line, and return without looking back.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite"], "teachers": ["tch:prajapati"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text katharudra-upanisad 1 (rite)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1 (rite) located in the e-text; the passage matches the paraphrase.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:katharudra-upanisad:17-22", "source": "src:katharudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "17-22"}, "paraphrase": "The five sheaths are explained and the Self is beyond them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text katharudra-upanisad 17-22"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 17-22 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'asthi-snāyvādirūpo'yaṃ śarīraṃ bhāti dehinām | yo'yamannamayo hyātmā bhāti sarva śarīriṇaḥ || 17 || tataḥ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:katharudra-upanisad:37-41", "source": "src:katharudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "37-41"}, "paraphrase": "Consciousness is sevenfold — pure, Īśvara, jīva, the knower, the means of knowing, the known and the result; all are the one consciousness.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text katharudra-upanisad 37-41"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 37-41 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'śuddhamīśvaracaitanyaṃ jīva-caitanyameva ca | pramātā ca pramāṇaṃ ca prameyaṃ ca phalaṃ tathā || 37 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
